WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:08.150
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:14.660
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.490
It's my day!

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:27.070
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:34.480
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:41.850
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:49.260
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:55.030
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:02.170
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:09.680
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.820
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.890
I just want to walk

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.420
Not on tip-toe

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:26.400
Not downcast, either

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:35.300
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:41.740
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:44.010
It's my day!

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.530
<i>It's great about you and Domyoji.</i>

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.300
<i>Tsukushi, you really think so?</i>

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.070
<i>Of course.</i>

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:47.150
<i>I thought I'd put Domyoji behind me.</i>

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:49.950
<i>But when I saw that...</i>

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:00.930
<i>It felt like something shattered
inside of me.</i>

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:09.070
<i>Falling to pieces...</i>

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:13.670
<i>And no one could put the pieces
of my heart back together.</i>

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:24.180
"Open Up Your Heart"

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:26.620
I'm home...

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.360
Welcome back...

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:48.670
What are you doing?

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:51.980
Well... you see...

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:54.950
What's going on here?!

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:57.720
Wait...

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.790
You got another loan?

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.190
You're running away
from debt collectors?!

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.120
No, we're not, Tsukushi.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.530
We didn't tell you to keep you
from worrying.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.560
We're at the end of our rope.

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:16.800
I know. I live with you.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:21.340
Your dad can't find any job
here in Tokyo.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.380
I have a friend who's a fisherman
in the countryside.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:30.420
He offered us a live-in job.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:33.750
So we're moving
to a fishing village?

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.960
Dad is going to be a <i>fisherman?!</i>

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:52.440
Are you okay with this, Dad?

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.180
Tsukushi, you must have faith in me.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:02.410
A fisherman's life is wild and romantic.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.520
It's a treacherous life ruled
by the sea and weather.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:09.120
Dad...

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:13.380
Besides, I always watch
"Let's Go Fishing" on TV,

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.730
so I know exactly
what to expect.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.600
<i>I'm not convinced at all.</i>

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:24.340
When I told him about it a week ago,
he was so eager to do it.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:26.600
We decided to take
the offer yesterday.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:30.010
I've never seen your dad so excited.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:35.350
<i>He's not so much eager, as deluded.</i>

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:38.020
<i>Life's not so easy...</i>

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:39.920
Besides...

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.490
Since we're living with them,

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:46.260
we should be able to send you
your tuition.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:53.930
Then, all you'll need to cover
is rent and living expenses.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:58.670
That should make things
easier for you.

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:04.440
That's right.
We really were a burden on you.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:08.750
I'll do my very best.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.370
It's so unfair!
I want to stay in Tokyo, too.

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:32.870
You're still in junior high.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.340
You'll go to school out there
until you graduate!

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:36.710
What?!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:39.340
You mean
only I'm staying behind?

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:41.110
Of course!

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:43.870
You managed to get into
such an expensive school.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:46.350
If you leave now,
you'll never get back in again!

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.730
We'll be back after I've earned
a small fortune.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:54.430
You won't be alone for long.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:56.230
That's right. Hang in there!

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.700
<i>"Hang in there"?</i>

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:03.600
<i>What's with them deciding all this for me?</i>

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:07.530
Now, let's get to work.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.040
Okay.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:13.640
Since your shoes are on,
go buy us some tape, Tsukushi.

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:14.880
One that's on sale!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:19.150
<i>Everything's gone haywire
since last night.</i>

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.020
<i>What's happening to my life?</i>

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:37.570
Tsukushi... I'm a little worried
about leaving you all alone.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.240
You'd better! That's how parents
are supposed to feel!

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:43.010
You didn't tell me anything.
Everything's all too sudden!

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:45.980
If we didn't do something...

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:51.780
we thought you wouldn't be able
to have Domyoji here.

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:53.580
You think I want to?!

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:02.660
<i>I feel like Urashima Taro when he returned
from the undersea palace...</i>

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.790
<i>After all that's happened
since last night...</i>

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:14.110
<i>nothing would surprise me.</i>

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:22.100
<i>I suppose, if I think about it,</i>

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:25.980
<i>life should be easier since I don't
have to support my family.</i>

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:33.060
<i>Yes. I'll be free of my no-privacy life
in that little apartment.</i>

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:37.600
<i>This may actually be good for me.</i>

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:39.660
<i>That's right!</i>

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:44.270
<i>Breakfast will be caf・au lait
and croissants,</i>

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:46.770
<i>instead of miso soup
and fermented soy beans.</i>

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:49.370
<i>I'll use a gingham place mat...</i>

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.150
<i>And I'll have potted ivy
on the windowsill.</i>

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:08.990
<i>You feel bad because it was Tsukasa.</i>

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:12.860
<i>No, that's not it!</i>

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:17.800
<i>I feel light as a wafer right now.</i>

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:31.840
Why do you two have to
butt into my thoughts?!

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:34.480
Quit hanging around in my head...

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:34.420
Mom... That girl...

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.750
Shh... Don't look at her.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.750
This is my private world!

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.960
They're stuck like glue to my head.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:03.680
<i>Stop it! Don't come in!
Please leave me alone!</i>

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:08.390
<i>If I looked it square in the face...</i>

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:18.530
<i>I know I'd learn something important.</i>

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:24.340
<i>But I'm stubborn, and I want 
to pretend I don't notice it.</i>

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.280
You're living alone?!

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:49.530
Yeah. My life's a rollercoaster.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:53.750
Things got that rough
for your folks?

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:54.800
You could say that.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:56.500
If we kept on like we were,

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:59.640
my brother wouldn't be able
to go to high school.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:04.510
If I quit Eitoku,
we would've been able to manage.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:09.350
"Not even if you died,"
was their only answer.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:13.250
Will you be okay
living alone, Tsukushi?

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:17.260
I'd be lying
if I said I wasn't scared...

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:20.960
but I think I've come to accept it.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:11.110
So much has happened
since I entered high school.

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:16.050
I guess I've gotten used to
all my "accidents."

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:19.580
Tsukushi...

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:23.850
I might not be of much help...

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:27.510
but you can lean on me when you feel
like you can't take it.

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:30.090
Thanks, I'll do that.

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:38.570
<i>But I really do feel lonely.</i>

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:46.600
<i>With things with Domyoji
still unresolved,</i>

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:49.880
<i>being left all alone
makes me so anxious.</i>

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:14.240
<i>But I can't keep saying that.</i>

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:18.110
Goodbye. We'll come and check up
on you from time to time.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.580
Be sure you lock up okay?

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.340
I will. Good luck, Dad.

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:26.450
Leave it to me!
I'll send you 500,000 yen a month.

00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:28.550
<i>500 THOUSAND...?</i>

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:30.890
I'll look forward to it.

00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:36.960
See you, Sis. I swear I'll be back
to enter high school.

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:40.130
Okay! Time for a fresh start!

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:09.090
<i>If I believe in it enough,
I'll be fine.</i>

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:13.730
<i>I'm strong in the face of adversity!</i>

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:24.430
<i>Still...</i>

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:25.840
Tsukushi!

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.050
Kazuya!

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:32.020
Is it true your folks have moved
to the country?

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:33.650
Yeah...

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:36.890
I'll be living alone
without a care.

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:41.630
But I worry...
A girl living alone...

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.400
It's Domyoji's bunch.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:50.470
Yikes!

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:57.540
Tsukushi!

00:14:58.540 --> 00:14:59.310
Hey, Makino...

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:02.980
What are you doing there?

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:04.380
<i>Oh, no...</i>

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:08.050
Oh, uh... well...

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:20.160
I hear you went with Rui and Tsukasa
to that monkey's villa.

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:23.740
H-h-how did you...?

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:26.300
Is it true, Tsukushi?

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:30.110
And you practically drowned in the bath
and were saved by Rui.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:31.110
In the bath?!

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:35.880
T-that was an emergency...
It couldn't be helped.

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:42.120
Blabbermouth!

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:44.360
You didn't have to tell them that!

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:46.090
I didn't tell them anything.

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:47.090
Oh?

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:49.930
Rui told us.

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:53.630
<i>Rui Hanazawa!</i>

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:55.900
So how did it go?

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:57.840
With the monkey girl?

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:03.040
There's nothing to talk about.

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:12.420
You don't have to be shy.

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:15.190
Butt out!
Just say whatever you want.

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:16.950
H-hey, Tsukasa!

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:28.070
Tsukushi!

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:30.540
How could you, when you have me!

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:54.230
<i>I don't think I'll be able to escape
this pain any time soon.</i>

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:06.600
<i>The only place I can run to...</i>

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:09.310
<i>...is there.</i>

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:20.920
Oh... It's you.

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.500
Why'd you go and tell
Nishikado and Mimasaka?

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:31.830
I was so embarrassed.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:35.030
Why not? It was the truth.

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:39.370
It may be the truth,
but some things shouldn't be told.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:50.320
You like to stuff everything
inside of you like that, huh?

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:56.050
Why don't you just be honest, for once?

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:13.300
How long are you going to pretend
you don't feel what you do?

00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:15.390
You and Tsukasa...

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:16.010
Shut up!

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.610
What about you?

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:27.220
You came running back from Paris...
from Shizuka.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:39.700
I'm sorry, I...

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:42.600
Something precious is standing
right before you.

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:47.640
You can just reach out
and grasp it...

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:52.110
But you don't even try. How can you
possibly understand how I feel?

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:18.000
<i>If I reach out...</i>

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:28.980
<i>But it's too late.</i>

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:46.060
So Tsukasa went
to the Okawaharas' villa?

00:19:47.030 --> 00:19:50.770
What worries me is that
Tsukushi Makino was with them.

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:02.210
It seems we'll have to
put a stop to that girl.

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:12.460
Tsukasa...

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:20.970
You don't have to do
Mother's bidding too, you know.

00:20:30.170 --> 00:20:34.750
I don't want you to have to
go through what I did.

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:37.980
I know...

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:51.260
Sis... Thanks.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:55.670
<i>Tsukasa?!</i>

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:19.560
<i>Why don't you just be honest, for once?</i>

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:27.870
<i>If I could do that,
I'd probably feel better.</i>

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:33.810
<i>But I still don't know how...</i>

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:38.440
<i>How can I be honest with myself?</i>

00:21:58.180 --> 00:22:04.780
Will I ever make it that far?

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:09.530
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:19.000
Some day, the whole world

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:24.810
will have its eyes on me.

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:32.560
Yeah, after our graduation ceremony

00:22:32.560 --> 00:22:38.180
we all wrote our dreams on the wall.

00:22:38.180 --> 00:22:44.800
A lot of time has passed since then

00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:51.200
but I'm just the same as I was on that day!

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:58.100
Keep trying your best! 
Wishes can come true!

00:22:58.100 --> 00:23:06.980
Let's keep running down
the road we believe in!

00:23:08.260 --> 00:23:14.890
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:14.890 --> 00:23:20.950
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:21.490 --> 00:23:28.210
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:31.600
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:31.600 --> 00:23:37.470
I already made it this far, after all.

00:23:46.190 --> 00:23:48.090
I'm living all alone now.

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:50.360
Since he returned
from Shigeru's villa...

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:52.260
...Domyoji's been acting weird.

00:23:52.800 --> 00:23:55.900
I hear Rui Hanazawa's 
violin again after so long.

00:23:56.430 --> 00:23:57.300
And...

00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:00.700
What? I can't believe it!

00:24:01.670 --> 00:24:04.570
Hana Yori Dango:
"Hurricane Approaching!!"

00:24:05.140 --> 00:24:07.980
This is a dream. It has to be!
